<!-- An edge node (conf/edge/README.md; plans/archive/Edge-Node.md): the production conf for a small cloud instance in
    front of a local node, which dials it and keeps one link open. It gives the local node web access (its host names,
    passthrough or terminate), an SSH tunnel, delegated calls, the queue and replication, mr-pass's sites with the local
    node as their authority, mail, chat webhooks and MMS files, the media and TURN of its calls, SIP trunks and outside
    phones, and XMPP clients' ports. The local node sets itself up with its System › Edge Node wizard, which reads what
    this node offers and sends its part (System › Edge Clients shows it); each section below says what this node needs
    for that area.
    Build, archive and run with the release flag of ./moq: the Maximal package, or Enterprise with an external database;
    both have the link. The runtime has the base components and mr-pass only (./moq component-get edge). Per-host
    settings (names, addresses, ports) go in .env, which an upgrade keeps. -->
<moqui-conf xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/moqui-conf-3.xsd">
    <default-property name="instance_purpose" value="production"/>
    <!-- takes links from paired local nodes on the HTTPS listener, told from browsers by ALPN; System › Edge Clients
        makes pairing codes, lists the paired nodes, pings and revokes them -->
    <default-property name="node_role" value="front_edge"/>
    <!-- rate limits, connection limits and bans by client address, run before anything goes down a link. With a proxy
        in front, name it in webapp_trusted_proxies (.env): a client-ip-header with no trusted proxies is ignored -->
    <default-property name="webapp_web_protection" value="true"/>

    <!-- The link and web access (.env): webapp_http_host, this node's public name. The HTTPS listener needs a WebPKI
        certificate in runtime/cert, which local nodes check when they pair; no TLS-terminating proxy in front, since the
        link needs ALPN and client certificates end to end. A local node dials 443 unless its edge node address has a
        port, and the listener binds webapp_https_listen_port (8443 by default): bind 443 (docs/Run-Deploy.md, Listen
        ports and URL ports) or give the port in the address. The links use this node's own key, edge_link_key,
        generated into .env at the first start: a renewed web certificate does not touch them, a changed key means every
        local node must pair again. edge_public_addresses: this node's public IPv4 and IPv6 addresses, comma-separated,
        which the wizard checks the local node's A and AAAA records against.
        A host name's mode is set on the local node (the wizard, or Edge Clients by hand). Passthrough, the default: this
        node reads the name before any TLS and sends the connection down the link with a PROXY header; the local node
        ends the TLS with its own certificate, and while the link is down the connection is refused. Terminate: this node
        ends the TLS with its own certificate for the name and forwards each request, and while the link is down shows an
        offline page (503), the page at edge_offline_page when set. -->

    <!-- SSH (.env): edge_ssh_tunnel_port (and edge_ssh_tunnel_host, empty for every address) takes SSH connections for
        the local node's SSH server (its ssh_port), each admitted by web protection first, while one local node is
        linked. With several, each gets a port of its own: a moqui.edge.EdgePort row (System › Edge Clients › Ports). -->

    <!-- PASS (plans/archive/Edge-Node.md §5.5): mr-pass here calls its local node as the PASS authority over gRPC down
        the link, with no client secret (the link authenticates it). Set pass_backend_web_url in .env to the local node's
        web address through this node (one of its host names), for the SSO front channel. While the link is down every
        PASS page fails as unavailable. -->
    <default-property name="pass_backend_url" value="edge:"/>

    <!-- XMPP (docs/interfaces/XMPP.md, Behind an edge node): no XMPP server runs here; XMPP clients' ports tunnel to the
        local node whose XMPP domain each connection names (the TLS server name, or the stream's to), which ends their
        TLS with its certificates for the domain. One pair of ports takes every paired node's domain. Set in .env:
                                     <default-property name="edge_xmpp_port" value="5222"/>
                                     <default-property name="edge_xmpp_tls_port" value="5223"/>
        (and edge_xmpp_host). _xmpp-client._tcp and _xmpps-client._tcp in public DNS name this node. -->

    <!-- Mail (docs/interfaces/Mail-Inbound.md, The edge node as the gateway: each setting, the DNS to publish and the
        Postfix alternative): the MTA in moqui (E5b). The SMTP listener takes port 25 from the internet itself (internet
        mode): set smtp_listen_port 25, smtp_listen_host 0.0.0.0 (or :: for IPv6 too) and smtp_hostname (the MX name,
        also the authserv-id) in .env. STARTTLS with the web certificate, the limits per address below, SPF, DKIM, DMARC
        and ARC checked, Rspamd's verdict when mail_rspamd_url is set. RCPT TO is answered from the local node's
        replicated accounts, so an unknown address is refused while it is away too, and each message is queued for it.
        Mail the local node sends through an EmailServer with smtpHost edge: is DKIM-signed here (mail_dkim_key, made
        into .env on first use) and delivered to each domain's MX, from bounce+(item)@ the domain
        edge_mail_bounce_domain names (set it in .env, with its MX here).
        Postfix and Rspamd beside it instead (E5a): in .env edge_mail_mta=postfix, smtp_internet=false,
        smtp_listen_port=10024 and smtp_allowed_addresses=127.0.0.1,::1, and protocol="lmtp" on the smtp-server below;
        mail out is relayed to Postfix on edge_mail_relay_port. -->
    <default-property name="edge_mail_mta" value="moqui"/>
    <default-property name="smtp_internet" value="true"/>
    <default-property name="edge_mail_relay_host" value="127.0.0.1"/>
    <default-property name="edge_mail_relay_port" value="10025"/>
    <smtp-server max-connections="100" max-connections-per-ip="5" connections-per-minute="30"/>

    <!-- Chat bridges and SMS (docs/interfaces/SMS.md): a network's webhook URL is this node's,
        /channels/{chatBridgeId}/webhook. The signature is checked with the local node's replicated bridge and the
        request queued for it; the files of the texts the local node sends (MMS) are served here at
        /channels/{id}/media/. On the local node, channels_public_url is this node's address (the wizard sets it). -->
    <default-property name="channels_webhooks_enabled" value="true"/>

    <!-- Calls (docs/interfaces/WebRTC.md, The edge node as media node; TURN.md, On an edge node): this node is the media
        node of its local node's calls, and their TURN. Set rtc_public_address in .env to this node's public address: the
        media socket binds every address, and does not start without it. Recordings are queued to the local node in
        segments of at most call_recording_segment_mb (32 at most, under the queue's 64 MiB content cap). Open UDP 10000
        (media), UDP and TCP 3478 (TURN) and the relay range turn_relay_ports (49152-65535). -->
    <default-property name="rtc_media_port" value="10000"/>
    <default-property name="rtc_media_host" value="0.0.0.0"/>
    <default-property name="turn_port" value="3478"/>
    <default-property name="call_recording_segment_mb" value="16"/>

    <!-- SIP (docs/interfaces/SIP.md, Behind an edge node): trunks and outside phones reach this node's SIP engine, whose
        media is the call media above. Set in .env to take them (each listener is off until its port is set):
                                     <default-property name="sip_port" value="5060"/>
                                     <default-property name="sip_tls_port" value="5061"/>
                                     <default-property name="sip_host" value="0.0.0.0"/>
                                     <default-property name="sip_public_address" value="(this node's address)"/>
        and sip_registrar_enabled=true for desk and soft phones outside the office (they sign in only while the local
        node, which checks their passwords, is reachable). The trunks are the local node's, replicated here, so they
        register and take calls while it is away; a call then gets its number's replicated fallback, else 480, so set the
        trunk provider's failover number too. Open sip_port (UDP, TCP), sip_tls_port (TCP) and sip_rtp_ports (UDP,
        20000-20999), to the trunk provider's addresses where it publishes them. -->

    <!-- Backups: the link's queue (what waits for a local node that is away) is the only data here that matters. The
        nightly backup_EmbeddedDatabase_daily job is paused in the seed data; this sets it running at each boot (false
        pauses it). Give it a mirror on System › Operations › Jobs to keep a copy off this host (docs/Run-Deploy.md,
        Backups). It backs up the embedded database only: with an external one it logs that it skipped, and the
        database is backed up with its own tools. -->
    <default-property name="embedded_db_backup_scheduled" value="true"/>

    <entity-facade crypt-pass="${entity_ds_crypt_pass}" query-stats="true"/>

    <!-- How work crosses the link (plans/archive/Edge-Node.md §5.2): what waits for a local node that is away is kept 14
        days (both nodes should keep the same period), and at most 1 GB of it for each paired node (a pairing's own
        EdgeClient.queueMaxMegabytes in place of it, plans/Edge-Node2.md §4.1); then its oldest fails, logged. A payload
        is at most 1 MiB, and a larger body (up to 64 MiB, a mail message) goes as its content. What the edge node
        delegates, the queue kinds and the sets a local node replicates are in MoquiDefaultConf.xml, read by both ends,
        with grants for _EDGE_ (the EDGE_DELEGATE artifact group); an entry may wait less than the link for its answer,
        as SIP's routing does while the caller's phone rings:
            <delegate service="org.moqui.call.VoiceServices.receive#PhoneCall" timeout-seconds="7"/>
        To check a delegated call end to end, list org.moqui.edge.EdgeServices.echo#Delegate on both nodes.
        Balancing a pairing's pool of local nodes (plans/Edge-Node2.md §4.4): a terminate host's requests stay on the
        member their session cookie hashes to (sticky-cookie, the session cookie; a host's own with add#EdgeHost
        stickyCookie); a member whose requests fail or time out set-aside-failures times in a row gets no new work for
        set-aside-seconds. -->
    <edge queue-retention-days="14" queue-max-megabytes="1024" queue-max-attempts="10" queue-retry-seconds="5"
            sticky-cookie="moqui.session" set-aside-failures="3" set-aside-seconds="30"/>
</moqui-conf>
